{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "נעברה נא בארצך", :translit "na'evrah na b'artzekha", :gloss "let us pass through your land"} {:he "אעברה נא", :translit "a'evrah na", :gloss "let me pass"} {:he "נסעה ונלכה", :translit "nis'ah v'nelkhah", :gloss "let us journey and let us go"} {:he "אחיך ישראל", :translit "akhikha yisra'el", :gloss "your brother Israel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast in wording: to Edom Moses says נעברה (first person plural), to Sihon אעברה (first person singular); Ba'al HaTurim links Edom's plural form to Esau's own plural speech."}], :frame {:text "When Jacob sends messengers to Esau he uses the plural cohortative: נסעה ונלכה (Genesis 33:12). Moses now addresses Edom as אחיך ישראל and similarly speaks in the plural — נעברה נא — echoing Jacob's diplomatic posture toward Esau recorded at Genesis 33:12.", :sources ["Genesis 33:12" "Numbers 20:17"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast in wording: to Edom Moses says נעברה (first person plural), to Sihon אעברה (first person singular); Ba'al HaTurim links Edom's plural form to Esau's own plural speech.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:15.452702430Z", :model "glm-5.2"}